---
import HomeLayout from '../../layouts/HomeLayout.astro';
import { beanReviews } from '../../data/bean-reviews';
import '../../styles/review.css';
import '../../styles/beans.css';
import '../../styles/bean-guides.css';

const date = '2026-10-21';
const path = '/coffee-beans/best-coffee-beans-for-french-press/';
const canonical = 'https://coffeedant.com' + path;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const local = (value: string) => base + value.replace(/^\//, '');
const title = 'Best Coffee Beans for French Press';
const description = 'Research-led US French press bean guide: four exact whole-bean coffees for dark coffee with milk, medium fruit, cream-friendly filter and decaf, with brew evidence and tradeoffs.';
const pickSpecs = [
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/blue-bottle-giant-steps/',best:'Dark press with milk',method:'Blue Bottle explicitly labels French press with milk and a 1:13 start',tradeoff:'The current full origin and process breakdown is absent',skip:'You want a light, clear, fruit-first cup',roast:'Dark',price:'Check live US price'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/peets-big-bang/',best:'Medium roast with fruit',method:'Peet’s names French press, pour-over and cold brew for this exact blend',tradeoff:'Its fruit-tart brief may not suit a low-acid dark-roast buyer',skip:'You want a fixed single-origin lot or very dark roast',roast:'Medium',price:'Check live US price'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/equator-blend/',best:'Coffee with cream',method:'Equator publishes a French press start near 1:15 for its house blend',tradeoff:'The blend changes by component and the press recipe is not a taste guarantee',skip:'You mainly need an espresso-specific shot recipe',roast:'Medium-dark',price:'Check live US price'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/blue-bottle-night-light-decaf/',best:'Decaf press',method:'Blue Bottle explicitly invites French press and espresso for its water-process decaf',tradeoff:'It suggests a heavier dose but gives no exact product-specific press ratio',skip:'You require a measured zero-caffeine guarantee',roast:'Medium label; darker prose',price:'Check live US price'}
];
const picks = pickSpecs.map((spec) => ({...spec, review: beanReviews.find((review) => review.slug === spec.slug)!}));
if (picks.some((pick) => !pick.review)) throw new Error('French press guide references a missing bean review');
const sections = [
  {id:'method',title:'Selection method: fit the cup, then the press',paragraphs:[
    'French press is immersion brewing. Coffee and water remain in contact before the plunger separates the grounds; the mesh retains more oils and fine particles than a paper filter. That makes body and sediment part of the buyer decision, not proof that dark beans are universally better. We selected four current US whole-bean products with a direct press recommendation or a roaster-published press recipe and a distinct reason to buy. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'The shortlist covers a dark milk-friendly cup, a medium fruit-led coffee, a house blend with cream and a water-process decaf. We required exact product identity, a current roaster page, a full Coffeedant review, a relevant brew path and a useful limitation. We excluded generic “best coffee” claims without a clear press use, expired price-led picks and products whose only support was an old tasting of a different lot. [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'These best-for labels are editorial judgments from documentation, not a Coffeedant cupping or a controlled ranking. Blue Bottle’s 1:13 for Giant Steps and Equator’s roughly 1:15 are different roaster starts. Try one small bag, keep the grind and dose documented, then adjust from your own cup instead of treating a published ratio as a score.'
  ]},
  {id:'brewing',title:'Use a press recipe, not a pour-over schedule',paragraphs:[
    'Blue Bottle’s French press guide advises a coarse grind because several minutes of immersion can overextract a fine grind. It separates the steep and decanting stage from the spiral pours on its dripper guide. Blue Bottle explicitly marks Giant Steps for press with milk at 1:13. Thirty grams of coffee to 390 grams of water preserves that ratio before adding milk; that arithmetic is a starting point, not a Coffeedant extraction. [1] [2]',
    'Equator’s house blend gives a press start near 1:15; 30 g to 450 g is a corresponding calculation. Peet’s Big Bang is press-recommended but the product page does not prescribe one exact press dose. Night Light invites press and asks for a heavier dose, without providing a fixed ratio. Do not manufacture precision for the latter two. Use the roaster’s device guide or a familiar press recipe, and change one variable at a time. [3] [4] [5]',
    'Decant the finished coffee when the recipe calls for it so grounds do not continue sitting in the drink. If your cup is gritty, inspect grinder particle distribution and pour technique before assuming a different bean will remove all sediment. If you want a very clean, bright cup, a paper-filter method may fit better than a press regardless of product.'
  ]},
  {id:'flavor',title:'Roaster notes point to four different directions',paragraphs:[
    'Blue Bottle gives Giant Steps cocoa, toasted marshmallow and graham cracker, with a dark roast and milk-friendly brief. Peet’s describes Big Bang as a medium coffee with fruit-tart character. Equator’s house blend mixes its own sweet, spiced and chocolate language with a cream-and-sugar role. Blue Bottle lists crème brûlée, vanilla and key lime for Night Light. These are attributed roaster notes, not flavors Coffeedant observed. [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'An older independent Giant Steps tasting found its press cup different from paper-filter cups; a 2026 Japanese Night Light account concerns a regional bag. The linked reviews show those sources and their limits. They do not establish a current US side-by-side comparison. The strongest recommendation here is about the documented role, not an invented sensory margin. [6] [7]',
    'A press with milk can mute fruit and emphasize a heavier impression, but the result depends on dose, water, grind and milk quantity. Hold those steady if comparing two bags. If you dislike citrus or berry cues, do not buy a fruit-described coffee on the assumption that a mesh filter will remove them.'
  ]},
  {id:'freshness',title:'Judge the delivered roast date and quantity',paragraphs:[
    'Product photographs are identity aids, not proof of the roast date or current component harvest. Two Blue Bottle review images here show Korean 250 g packaging because that is the available credited product image; the US reviews explicitly identify that difference. Buy using the US product selector and inspect the actual pack you receive. [2] [5]',
    'A 12 oz bag is about 340 g. At a 30 g press dose, it yields about eleven theoretical brews before dialing waste. If a household presses only on weekends, a large pack can age before it is used. Keep opened whole beans sealed, cool, dry and away from odors, then grind immediately before brewing. [8] [9]',
    'Recurring blends can change components while preserving a flavor target. Peet’s, Equator and Blue Bottle product names do not lock one farm or variety indefinitely. Record the bag’s roast date and any component panel; recheck the roaster page on a later order.'
  ]},
  {id:'value',title:'Compare delivered US bags, not subscription tiles',paragraphs:[
    'The checked storefronts exposed size, one-time and subscription controls in ways that did not yield a reliably comparable delivered price across all four exact whole-bean packs. This guide therefore gives no price ranking or unverified discount. Compare the current one-time US size, tax, shipping and stock in the cart you would actually use. [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'A low price per ounce is wasted if the pack sits open or the roast direction is wrong for the household. Giant Steps earns a first-bag trial when the goal is dark press with milk; Big Bang when medium fruit sounds welcome; Equator Blend when coffee with cream is the routine; Night Light when decaf is the requirement. A separate grinder and clean water affect every one of those outcomes.',
    'The press itself does not turn a bag into a substitute for a café espresso. If switching between espresso and press, use distinct grinder settings and ratios. Our separate espresso-and-drip guide and grinder reviews cover those decisions without pretending one recipe works everywhere.'
  ]}
];
const faqs = [
  {q:'Which pick has the clearest French press instruction?',a:'Blue Bottle labels Giant Steps for French press with milk and gives a 1:13 starting ratio. Equator Blend also has a press start near 1:15.'},
  {q:'Is dark roast required for French press?',a:'No. Press technique works across roast levels. This shortlist includes medium Peet’s Big Bang for a buyer who wants a fruit-led direction.'},
  {q:'Which bag is decaf?',a:'Blue Bottle Night Light Decaf is water-decaffeinated and explicitly positioned for French press. Decaf does not mean measured zero caffeine.'},
  {q:'Can I copy a pour-over recipe into a press?',a:'Use the press-specific grind, immersion and decanting steps. A dripper pour schedule and a press immersion ratio answer different brewing questions.'},
  {q:'Does milk change the best pick?',a:'It can change what a person notices. Giant Steps has explicit press-with-milk positioning; Equator Blend is described for cream and sugar. Coffeedant has not tasted either with milk.'},
  {q:'What if I dislike sediment?',a:'Use a consistent coarse grind and decant carefully. If you prefer a very clean cup, a paper-filter brewer may suit you better than any of these press picks.'},
  {q:'Are prices and tasting scores current?',a:'No numeric sensory score is assigned. Check the live US cart for size, stock, one-time price, tax and shipping before purchasing.'}
];
const sources = [
  ['Blue Bottle: French press method','https://bluebottlecoffee.com/brew-guides/french-press','Coarse grind, immersion and device-specific handling.'],
  ['Blue Bottle US: Giant Steps','https://bluebottlecoffee.com/us/eng/product/giant-steps','Dark roast, attributed notes, press with milk and 1:13.'],
  ['Peet’s US: Big Bang','https://www.peets.com/products/big-bang','Exact blend and French press use; current lot and stock require a fresh check.'],
  ['Equator US: Equator Blend','https://www.equatorcoffees.com/products/equator-blend','Cream-and-sugar role and separate French press guidance.'],
  ['Blue Bottle US: Night Light Decaf','https://bluebottlecoffee.com/us/eng/product/night-light-decaf','Water-decaf status and espresso-to-press positioning.'],
  ['Coffee Cantata: Giant Steps sample','https://coffeecantata.co/?p=6097','Older independent sample across brew methods; not a current-lot ranking.'],
  ['iAnswer: Night Light Decaf sample','https://note.com/ianswer_2022/n/nb49d95afe54','2026 Japanese regional bag; limited transfer to US.'],
  ['Blue Bottle: freshness','https://blog.bluebottlecoffee.com/posts/on-freshness','Roast-date context; not a universal best-before rule.'],
  ['Stumptown: opened-bean storage','https://support.stumptowncoffee.com/hc/en-us/articles/5568076789901-Where-should-I-store-my-coffee-In-the-freezer-On-the-counter','Independent roaster storage context.']
];
const cite = (p: string) => p.replace(/\[(\d+)\]/g, (_m,n) => '<a class="bean-cite" href="#s' + n + '" aria-label="Source ' + n + '">[' + n + ']</a>');
const author = {'@type':'Person',name:'Aleksandar Spasevski',jobTitle:'Editor, Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/about/',image:'https://coffeedant.com/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg'};
const schema = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[
  {'@type':'Article','@id':canonical+'#article',headline:title,description,genre:'Research-led coffee buying guide',inLanguage:'en-US',datePublished:date,dateModified:date,author,mainEntityOfPage:canonical,image:picks.map(p=>p.review.image),citation:sources.map(s=>s[1]),publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/'}},
  {'@type':'ItemList','@id':canonical+'#shortlist',name:title,itemListElement:picks.map((p,i)=>({'@type':'ListItem',position:i+1,name:p.review.roaster+' '+p.review.coffee,url:'https://coffeedant.com'+p.slug}))},
  {'@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:'https://coffeedant.com/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Coffee beans',item:'https://coffeedant.com/coffee-beans/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:title,item:canonical}]},
  {'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map(f=>({'@type':'Question',name:f.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:f.a}}))}
]};
---
<HomeLayout title={title + ' | Coffeedant'} description={description} canonicalPath={path} image={picks[0].review.image} imageAlt={picks[0].review.imageAlt} ogType="article" published={date} updated={date}>
  <main id="main-content" class="review-page bean-buying-guide" data-guide-kind="coffee-beans">
    <div class="review-shell">
      <nav class="review-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a><span>/</span><a href={local('/coffee-beans/')}>Coffee beans</a><span>/</span><span>French press</span></nav>
      <header class="bean-guide-header"><p class="review-overline">Coffee buying guide · research-led · United States</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="bean-lead">Choose the cup you actually press: dark coffee with milk, medium fruit, cream-friendly filter or decaf. Four exact bags have distinct evidence and limits.</p><aside class="review-author-card"><div class="review-author-head"><img src={local('/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg')} alt="Aleksandar Spasevski, editor at Coffeedant" width="46" height="46" /><div><strong>Aleksandar Spasevski</strong><small>Editor, Coffeedant</small></div></div><p>Published and checked <time datetime={date}>October 21, 2026</time> · US whole-bean context</p><p>I checked current roaster product and brew pages, independent sample context and the linked full reviews. I have not bought, brewed or tasted these coffees. Best-for labels are research-led buying judgments.</p></aside></header>
      <nav class="bean-jump" aria-label="Guide sections"><strong>Choose your press coffee</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={'#'+s.id}>{s.title}</a>)}<a href="#quick-compare">Quick comparison</a><a href="#picks">The picks</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
      <article class="bean-article">
        {sections.slice(0,2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">The buyer decision</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="quick-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Four defensible roles</p><h2>Quick comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable French press bean comparison"><table><caption>Exact US whole-bean products checked October 21, 2026; verify checkout prices</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Coffee</th><th scope="col">Best for</th><th scope="col">Roast</th><th scope="col">Think twice if</th></tr></thead><tbody>{picks.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.roaster} {p.review.coffee}</a></th><td>{p.best}</td><td>{p.roast}</td><td>{p.skip}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="picks"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Exact bags, stated use</p><h2>The four picks</h2></header><div class="bean-index-grid">{picks.map(p=><article class="bean-guide-pick"><img src={p.review.image} alt={p.review.imageAlt} width="360" height="360" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div><p class="review-overline">{p.best}</p><h3><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.roaster} {p.review.coffee}</a></h3><p><strong>Evidence:</strong> {p.method}.</p><p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> {p.tradeoff}.</p><p><strong>Skip if:</strong> {p.skip}.</p><p class="bean-credit"><a href={p.review.imageSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image: {p.review.roaster}</a>. {p.review.imageCredit}</p><a class="bean-guide-review-link" href={local(p.slug)}>Read the full review →</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="detailed-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Check the evidence, not just roast color</p><h2>Detailed comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable detailed French press comparison"><table><caption>Published brew roles and limitations; no Coffeedant tasting scores or verified price ranking</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Factor</th>{picks.map(p=><th scope="col"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.coffee}</a></th>)}</tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Best role</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.best}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Roaster brew evidence</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.method}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Roast direction</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.roast}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Main limit</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.tradeoff}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">US value</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.price}</td>)}</tr></tbody></table></div></section>
        {sections.slice(2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Make a repeatable choice</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="related"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Related buyer decisions</p><h2>When a press is only one brewer</h2></header><div class="bean-alternatives"><a href={local('/coffee-beans/best-coffee-beans-for-espresso-and-drip/')}><strong>Espresso and drip</strong><span>Pick one bag for two recipes without merging their grind settings.</span></a><a href={local('/coffee-beans/best-decaf-coffee-beans-by-brew-method/')}><strong>More decaf choices</strong><span>Compare decaf by method and process.</span></a><a href={local('/grinder/')}><strong>Grinder reviews</strong><span>Find a grinder that suits coarse immersion and any espresso switching.</span></a></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="methodology"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Evidence and limits</p><h2>How this guide was made</h2></header><div class="review-section-body"><p>We matched current exact US roaster pages with a distinct French press use case, a linked research-led full review, and a practical reason to skip each coffee. Older independent sample reports and owner comments inform uncertainty but do not rank current bags. Coffeedant did not buy, brew, taste or measure these coffees.</p><p>No delivered one-time US price was reliably comparable across all four selected pack controls on October 21, 2026. Check the active cart for size, order cadence, shipping, tax and stock. Affiliate links or seller offers do not determine best-for labels.</p></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="faq"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Quick answers</p><h2>French press bean FAQ</h2></header><div class="bean-faq">{faqs.map(f=><article><h3>{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="sources"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Trace the claims</p><h2>Sources</h2></header><ol class="review-source-list">{sources.map((s,i)=><li id={'s'+(i+1)}><a href={s[1]} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{s[0]} ↗</a><p>{s[2]} Checked October 21, 2026.</p></li>)}</ol></section>
        <section class="final-verdict"><p class="review-overline">The useful first bag</p><h2>Buy for your cup, then tune one press variable at a time</h2><p>Start with a small whole-bean pack, inspect the roast date, and keep your grind, dose, water and milk quantity documented. The delivered cup decides whether the same coffee deserves a larger order.</p><a class="review-buy-button review-buy-button-dark" href={local('/coffee-beans/')}>Explore all bean reviews →</a></section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />
</HomeLayout>
